```c
for (i = 0; i < PTE_PREFETCH_NUM; i++, spte++) {
    if (is_shadow_present_pte(*spte) || spte == sptep) {
        if (!start)
            continue;
        if (direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte) < 0)
            break;
        start = NULL;
    } else if (!start)
        start = spte;
}
```
Reason:
The loop iterates over the SPTEs, but if all preceding SPTEs are not present, it fails to prefetch any trailing SPTEs after the faulting GFN, leading to an increased number of guest page faults.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (start)
    direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte);
```
Reason:
This additional check after the loop ensures that if there are any trailing SPTEs that need to be prefetched (indicated by `start` being non-null), the `direct_pte_prefetch_many()` function is called to handle them, thus reducing the number of guest page faults.

